    "details": "<p><strong>Welcome to Horizon &mdash; by Hoollow!</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Horizon</strong> is an offline Software Development hackathon by <strong>Hoollow</strong>, built for students and young builders who want to turn ideas into working products.</p>\n<p>From building your first <strong>MVP online</strong> to competing in an intense <strong>24-hour offline development round in Delhi</strong>, Horizon is designed to take you beyond just coding &mdash; into <strong>problem-solving, product thinking, teamwork, and real-world execution</strong>.</p>\n<p>Whether you're a beginner exploring software development or an experienced builder, Horizon gives you a platform to <strong>build, compete, connect, and get recognized.</strong></p>\n<h2>About the Opportunity</h2>\n<p>Horizon is more than a conventional hackathon. It is a two-stage building experience focused on turning ideas into practical software solutions.</p>\n<p>Throughout the hackathon, participants will develop skills across:</p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>Software Development</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Product Thinking</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Project Management</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Problem Solving</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Teamwork &amp; Collaboration</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Innovation &amp; Execution</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Format</strong></p>\n<p>Horizon consists of <strong>two competitive rounds</strong>.</p>\n<h2>Round 1 &mdash; Online MVP Challenge</h2>\n<p>Participants will build and submit a <strong>Minimum Viable Product (MVP)</strong> based on the given theme.</p>\n<h3>Theme: AI with Education</h3>\n<p><strong>Problem Statement:</strong></p>\n<p>Teams can explore ideas across areas such as:</p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Education</li>\n<li>Productivity</li>\n<li>Accessibility</li>\n<li>Communication</li>\n<li>Local Services</li>\n<li>Sustainability</li>\n<li>Student Life</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There are <strong>no restrictions on your technology stack or development tools</strong>. Teams are encouraged to use the technologies they are most comfortable with, including AI tools.</p>\n<h3>Submission Requirements</h3>\n<p>Your submission should include:</p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Project description</li>\n<li>Working MVP</li>\n<li><strong>2&ndash;3 minute demo video</strong></li>\n<li><strong>GitHub repository</strong></li>\n<li>Live demo, if available</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Projects will be evaluated based on factors such as:</p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Innovation</li>\n<li>Core functionality</li>\n<li>Feasibility</li>\n<li>Problem understanding</li>\n<li>Execution</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Shortlisting</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Top 50 teams</strong> from Round 1 will be shortlisted for the offline round.</p>\n<p>However, only the <strong>first 30 shortlisted teams to confirm their participation</strong> will secure their Round 2 spot.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &mdash; In-Person Delhi Hackathon</strong></p>\n<p>The shortlisted teams will come together in <strong>New Delhi</strong> for an intensive <strong>24-hour offline development challenge</strong>.</p>\n<p>This is where Horizon gets serious.</p>\n<p>Teams will receive a <strong>new problem statement/challenge in person at the venue</strong> and will be required to build, adapt, or extend their solution within the given timeframe.</p>\n<p>The round will test:</p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Speed of execution</li>\n<li>Technical ability</li>\n<li>Product thinking</li>\n<li>Creativity</li>\n<li>Team coordination</li>\n<li>Problem solving</li>\n<li>Scalability</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The exact venue and detailed instructions will be shared with selected participants.</p>\n<p><strong>Who Can Participate?</strong></p>\n<p>Horizon is open to students and young builders interested in software development and innovation.</p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>Team participation</strong></li>\n<li>Teams must register through the official Horizon portal</li>\n<li>Beginners are welcome</li>\n<li>Participants can use any suitable technology stack</li>\n<li>AI-assisted development is allowed</li>\n<li>Projects must be original</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What You Get</strong></p>\n<p>Horizon isn't just about winning a prize. Participants get access to opportunities that can continue beyond the hackathon.</p>\n<h3>For the Top Performers</h3>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><strong>#1&ndash;#3:</strong> CodeCrafters VIP Memberships worth <strong>$1000+</strong></li>\n<li><strong>#1&ndash;#2:</strong> High-value credits from <strong>InterviewBuddy</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Participant Rewards</h3>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li><code dir=\"ltr\"><strong>.xyz</strong></code> <strong>Domains:</strong> Top 50 participants</li>\n<li><strong>Swags:</strong> Top 100 participants</li>\n<li><strong>Certificates co-branded with GeeksforGeeks:</strong> All participants</li>\n<li><strong>Coupon Codes:</strong> All Round 2 participants</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Career Opportunities</h3>\n<p><strong>Internship Interview Opportunities</strong></p>\n<p>All Round 2 participants will get the opportunity to interview with <strong>Hoollow and associated early-stage startups</strong>.</p>\n<h3>Get Featured on India's Got Intelligence</h3>\n<p>All Round 2 participants will get a <strong>chance to be interviewed on India's Got Intelligence</strong>, giving them an opportunity to showcase their projects, share their building journey, and gain additional exposure.</p>\n<p><strong>Why Participate?</strong></p>\n<p>Horizon gives you the chance to:</p>\n<p><strong>Build &rarr; Compete &rarr; Get Recognized &rarr; Connect &rarr; Grow</strong></p>\n<p>Whether you're looking to:</p>\n<ul data-spread=\"false\">\n<li>Build your first serious project</li>\n<li>Strengthen your development portfolio</li>\n<li>Work under real-world constraints</li>\n<li>Meet other ambitious builders</li>\n<li>Explore internship opportunities</li>\n<li>Get your project in front of a wider audience</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Horizon gives you a place to do it.</p>\n<p><strong>About Hoollow</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Hoollow</strong> is a youth-driven technology and builder ecosystem focused on helping young people <strong>build, connect, and create real-world impact</strong>.</p>\n<p>Through hackathons, communities, startup programs, and builder-focused initiatives, Hoollow creates opportunities for young developers, founders, and innovators to move from <strong>learning &rarr; building &rarr; launching</strong>.</p>",
